{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1079496034"}, "name":{"label":"Tankbot#0001"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2020-01-07T20:46:04-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0"}, "id":{"label":"5374683951"}, "title":{"label":"Great but short"}, "content":{"label":"I was really fond of this game, it was a very artistic and beautiful game with its simplicity and lighting. The controls were fine but I think they could be improved. What I didn’t like most about this game was the fact I beat it in 2 hours while idle watching TV. It was very nice, very puzzling, but short for my taste. The graphics are actually surprising as it was a mobile game made out of legos.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1441636691&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id499500131"}, "name":{"label":"LucasDestroyerofWorlds"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2020-01-07T19:14:40-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0"}, "id":{"label":"5374449710"}, "title":{"label":"beautiful, but GameCenter"}, "content":{"label":"This is more Apple Arcade than Lego.\n\nI started a file on my Apple TV, and assumed that when I access the game on my iPhone it would start from where I left off.\nBut it started a fresh game, both logged into the same GameCenter.\n\nThis has continually been something which has stopped me from enjoying a lot of games in Arcade.\n\nCan I or can I not move between devices on the same GameCenter account?\nWhat’s the point in having this service if the game doesn’t stay the same way on every device.\n\nApple, either abandon GameCenter or stay on it, make it simpler and easier to understand.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1441636691&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id37273313"}, "name":{"label":"BF261C5E"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2020-01-07T15:26:37-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0"}, "id":{"label":"5373844843"}, "title":{"label":"Love it! Want some more of it!"}, "content":{"label":"I feel like this is LEGO Heroica crossed with a LEGOPunk universe. First off, you must have a spirit of imagination and experimentation to play. Lacking these characteristics/skills, you’ll probably hate it. But... If you like to experiment, are imaginative, and LOVE LEGO. This will be a fun, casual, puzzler sandbox with a sweet story told without words.\n\nKudos to Apple for producing this and kudos to LEGO group for making a fine game in-house!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1441636691&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
